lay T4: Discarding from your T4 triplet would break a potential pung/kong, which is not advisable.\n\nGiven the unseen counts and exposed melds, you have good potential in Bamboo suit (B1, B2 pairs) and some in Characters. To maintain flexibility and maximize chance of completing hand, discard the most isolated tile that doesn't break promising combinations.\n\nReason: T3 is the most isolated tile\u2014it has limited chow possibilities (needs T1/T2 or T2/T4) and with T4 triplet, it's less likely to form a sequence. Discarding T3 keeps your pairs (W3, B1, B2) and triplet (T4) intact, and retains W8 which might connect with drawn W7/W9. Also, T3 discard is relatively safe given T3 has 3 unseen but some have been used in melds. This move maintains multiple routes to completion (pungs from pairs, sequences from W8 or Bamboo tiles).\n\nAnswer: Play T3"}
